ref":"p57-img1","page":57}]},{"path":"p58","title":"Look & Learn:","level":1,"page":58,"paragraphs":["Look & Learn:","Watch as We:","•","Navigate to Setup > Configure Documents > Manage","Custom Fields","•","Click the CSV Values Import / Export tab and discuss the","following: o","Requests o","Import Instructions o","Recent Activity","Importing and Exporting"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p58-img1","page":58}]},{"path":"p59","title":"Guided Activity:","level":1,"page":59,"paragraphs":["Guided Activity:","Let’s Do This Together:","•","Export Values for Fixed Asset Category","•","Review the resulting spreadsheet and: o","Leave the first value as-is o","Change just the CustomFieldValueDescription for the second o","Edit the remaining rows to add the following Values :","•","Heavy Trucks","•","Furniture","•","Appliances","•","Recreational Equipment","•","Machine Components","•","Others if you want","Importing and Exporting"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p59-img1","page":59}]},{"path":"p60","title":"Guided Activity:","level":1,"page":60,"paragraphs":["Guided Activity:","Let’s Do This Together:","•","Validate the file you just edited","•","Address any errors or warnings, if needed","•","Validate again if necessary, or Import","•","Create additional Parent/Child Value relationships","Importing and Exporting"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p60-img1","page":60}]},{"path":"p61","title":"One-Minute Synopsis","level":1,"page":61,"paragraphs":["One-Minute Synopsis","Custom Fields in JAGGAER Indirect","In Your Course Workbook:","In your own words, write down a brief synopsis of","custom fields in JAGGAER Indirect.","Update Your Task List!"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p61-img1","page":61}]},{"path":"p62","title":"Custom Fields","level":1,"page":62,"paragraphs":["Custom Fields","On your phone or laptop, go to","quizlet.live"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p62-img1","page":62}]},{"path":"p63","title":"Lessons in This Class","level":1,"page":63,"paragraphs":["Lessons in This Class","Custom Fields and System Documents","•","Significance of Custom Fields","•","Configuring Custom Fields","•","Importing and Exporting Custom Fields","•","System Documents","•","General Document Configuration Settings","•","Configuring P2P Documents","•","Configuring Commodity Codes"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p63-img1","page":63}]},{"path":"p64","title":"What We’ll Discuss in This Lesson:","level":1,"page":64,"paragraphs":["What We’ll Discuss in This Lesson:","General Document Configuration Settings","Lesson Topics:","•","System Documents o","Shopping Cart / Requisition Document o","Purchase Order Document o","Invoice and Other Documents","•","Document Configuration Options","•","Document Organization / Layout","•","Document Visibility"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p64-img1","page":64}]},{"path":"p65","title":"Key Terms","level":1,"page":65,"paragraphs":["Key Terms","Shopping Cart","The Cart shows items a shopper","wants – but has not yet formally","requested.","Requisition","The Requisition is the system","document created when they","submit their request for approval.","This is the document that travels","through the approvals process."],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p65-img1","page":65}]},{"path":"p66","title":"Key Terms","level":1,"page":66,"paragraphs":["Key Terms","Shopping Cart / Checkout / Requisition","Clients can configure shopping carts, checkout pages and","requisitions in their site, including:","•","The information they want to capture o","Header level o","Line level","•","Where items are located on the screen","•","Layout","Note: The “Requisition” Document is configured, and those settings","impact the “Cart” and are reflected on the “Checkout” page."],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p66-img1","page":66}]},{"path":"p67","title":"Key Terms","level":1,"page":67,"paragraphs":["Key Terms","Purchase Order","Once a cart is submitted and the approval process is complete,","a Purchase Order or “PO” is created. This document travels","through workflow and is seen by approvers."],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p67-img1","page":67}]},{"path":"p68","title":"Key Terms","level":1,"page":68,"paragraphs":["Key Terms","Faxes & Emails Sent to Suppliers","•","Suppliers not ‘enabled’ for electronic (cXML or EDI) delivery of orders","receive their orders from the system by fax or email","•","The Fax Document, which is on a separate tab in the PO configuration","section, formats this document","Note: This Document MUST be set up and activated before orders can go to","suppliers who are set to receive orders by fax, email or manual delivery!"],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p68-img1","page":68}]},{"path":"p69","title":"Key Terms","level":1,"page":69,"paragraphs":["Key Terms","Invoices","•","Invoices – electronic records of the ‘bill’ - are available to JI Accounts","Payable clients. They reflect what must be paid for, and how much is due.","•","The Invoice is managed by AP personnel and goes through workflow in","JAGGAER, then is sent to the ERP to say “pay this”."],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p69-img1","page":69}]},{"path":"p70","title":"Key Terms","level":1,"page":70,"paragraphs":["Key Terms","Credit Memos","•","Credit Memos reflect credits from a supplier after overpayment, returns,","etc.","•","Credit Memos are created the same way as invoices, but reflect credits","instead of money owed. They can: o","Be associated with a specific item and/or purchase","o","Be created as a general credit memo not associated with a specific purchase","•","The Credit Memo Document is configured on the same page as the","Invoice Document."],"tables":[],"figures":[{"ref":"p70-img1","page":70}]},{"path":"p71","title":"Setting Up Custom Fields for eProcurement","level":1,"page":71,"paragraphs":["Setting Up Custom Fields for eProcurement","Create and","configure the","Custom Field","Set up","potential","values","Specify","where the","field may","appear on","System","Documents","Set","Relationships","with other","Custom","Fields","Set